WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:01.176
- It should be pretty easy.

00:00:01.176 --> 00:00:02.158
Walking's easy.

00:00:02.158 --> 00:00:02.889
We're humans.

00:00:02.889 --> 00:00:04.744
My hearts were like, bro,

00:00:04.744 --> 00:00:06.524
what are you doing?

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:09.010
(island music)

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.407
- I looked up how far

00:00:15.407 --> 00:00:17.357
10,000 steps really is.

00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:18.664
- Actually quite a bit.

00:00:18.664 --> 00:00:20.092
- Almost five miles.

00:00:20.092 --> 00:00:21.673
- Eh, 10,000 is a little daunting.

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:23.584
- I do a lot of life change-type things,

00:00:23.584 --> 00:00:24.850
and I don't really commit.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.680
And in the end I don't have any results.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.787
Walking seems easy.

00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:30.085
Like I can walk.

00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:31.136
- I used to live in Chicago.

00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:32.229
I used to walk all the time.

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:33.163
When I was your age,

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:34.460
I walked three miles to work

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.516
in the snow.

00:00:35.516 --> 00:00:36.720
- I'm sitting at my desk.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.955
It gets really hard to
stay active and fit.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:41.476
- I don't have the best sleep schedule.

00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:42.776
Exercise is something that

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.075
just goes out the window.

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:45.863
- I'm always telling me
I gotta get exercise.

00:00:45.863 --> 00:00:47.854
I think it's time that
I get some exercise.

00:00:47.854 --> 00:00:49.849
- I feel like my body was healthier

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.230
when I walked a lot more.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.141
Although I did eat a
lot more frozen pizzas.

00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:56.164
(island music)

00:00:57.284 --> 00:00:59.243
- If I missed 10,000 steps,

00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:00.826
I owe $10.

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:02.436
- I give that to charity.

00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:04.309
- If I miss 100,000 steps,

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:05.376
I owe $100.

00:01:05.376 --> 00:01:07.212
- I don't plan on giving a lot of money

00:01:07.212 --> 00:01:08.596
to charity for this.

00:01:08.596 --> 00:01:09.727
Maybe there will be a day

00:01:09.727 --> 00:01:10.914
when I'm feeling generous,

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:12.498
and I will want to do nothing.

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.663
- Ooh. A fitbit.

00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:15.897
- Dutu dududu dutu.

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:17.235
- Alright.

00:01:17.235 --> 00:01:18.128
I love it.

00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:18.861
- How cute.

00:01:18.861 --> 00:01:20.810
Where do I put this on my body?

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.755
(acoustic music)

00:01:23.195 --> 00:01:24.734
- I'm in Tennessee.

00:01:24.824 --> 00:01:26.324
I walked so much,

00:01:26.324 --> 00:01:28.153
I found a river.
(water flowing)

00:01:28.153 --> 00:01:29.616
- Because it's crazy cold outside,

00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:31.442
I am not going out there,

00:01:31.442 --> 00:01:33.026
and I'm doing steps inside

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.815
with these guys.

00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:36.397
- I've been sick the last few days.

00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:37.525
It doesn't even matter

00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:38.789
'cause I didn't have my fitbit

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:40.922
in my pocket for the last five days.

00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:42.672
- I am walking at work.

00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:44.733
I decided to walk to lunch today.

00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:46.204
Look at that, we're gonna walk.

00:01:46.204 --> 00:01:47.739
We're gonna get a lot of steps in.

00:01:47.739 --> 00:01:49.252
- [Voiceover] Help me, come on guys.

00:01:49.252 --> 00:01:50.137
- Okay.

00:01:50.137 --> 00:01:51.367
- Let's go.

00:01:51.787 --> 00:01:53.184
(acoustic music)

00:01:57.184 --> 00:01:58.186
- Whoo!

00:01:58.186 --> 00:01:59.444
I am shocked by that

00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:00.284
but I'll take it.

00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:01.887
- I'm in second place.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:02.781
Me?

00:02:02.781 --> 00:02:04.084
- Heah.

00:02:04.084 --> 00:02:04.899
I'm at the bottom,

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:06.285
but I still have the
chance to turn it around.

00:02:06.285 --> 00:02:08.109
I have good excuses why I haven't

00:02:08.109 --> 00:02:09.495
hit those marks.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.909
It's 40 degrees outside and raining,

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:13.599
and it's been that way all day.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.379
- And you realize you've only done half

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:17.085
the amount of steps you're supposed to do.

00:02:17.085 --> 00:02:19.113
And your bed is so warm.

00:02:19.113 --> 00:02:21.420
- Umm. I don't know if
that's gonna happen.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.460
- It's really hard to go do it.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.202
- Having the dog is a great excuse

00:02:25.202 --> 00:02:27.493
'cause he gets me up
right away in the morning.

00:02:27.493 --> 00:02:28.412
- It forces me to walk.

00:02:28.412 --> 00:02:29.093
It really does.

00:02:29.093 --> 00:02:30.646
On weekends, I'm just laying in my bed,

00:02:30.646 --> 00:02:31.500
and it's like,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.517
I could just be walking.

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:35.076
I am walking in my neighborhood.

00:02:35.076 --> 00:02:35.928
I feel better.

00:02:35.928 --> 00:02:37.017
It would make me feel

00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:38.681
like I'm actually doing something.

00:02:39.861 --> 00:02:41.138
(acoustic music)

00:02:46.688 --> 00:02:48.357
- So guys, who isn't here right now?

00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:49.202
- Umm.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.388
- Jen.

00:02:50.388 --> 00:02:51.934
Isn't here.
- Sleeping.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.273
- She's at home right now.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.487
- What a piece of shit.

00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:55.879
- (laughing)

00:02:56.399 --> 00:02:58.107
(acoustic music)

00:02:59.827 --> 00:03:01.673
- No. Why?

00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:02.333
- (laughing)

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:03.343
- C'mon.

00:03:03.598 --> 00:03:05.192
(very hard breathing)
- Each step is so hard.

00:03:05.192 --> 00:03:06.691
My legs aren't like you

00:03:06.691 --> 00:03:07.779
in jeans Keith.

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:10.991
My hearts were like bro,

00:03:10.991 --> 00:03:12.463
what are you doing?

00:03:13.453 --> 00:03:14.682
(acoustic music)

00:03:22.672 --> 00:03:23.857
(wind blowing)

00:03:23.857 --> 00:03:25.654
- You know who didn't make it?

00:03:25.654 --> 00:03:26.466
Jen.

00:03:26.466 --> 00:03:27.565
- Jen tiger.

00:03:28.345 --> 00:03:29.641
(acoustic music)

00:03:35.911 --> 00:03:38.760
- I want to blame the influenza virus.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.377
There was a day that
I did wear the fitbit,

00:03:41.377 --> 00:03:42.961
and I walked 100 steps.

00:03:42.961 --> 00:03:44.300
(laughing)

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.330
- Being the biggest loser also means

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.051
that I'm the biggest philanthropist.

00:03:48.051 --> 00:03:49.514
I'm gonna give it to Alzheimer's.

00:03:49.514 --> 00:03:50.944
That's a good charity to give money to.

00:03:50.944 --> 00:03:52.643
- Well no, I just was last before

00:03:52.643 --> 00:03:54.787
so I was kind of anticipating being last.

00:03:54.787 --> 00:03:56.983
I did a lot better when
I was back at work.

00:03:56.983 --> 00:03:58.479
Emailing made me get up and walk.

00:03:58.479 --> 00:03:59.955
I think I'm gonna donate my money

00:03:59.955 --> 00:04:01.739
to a high school that's in Watts

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:03.245
for the neighborhood boys.

00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:04.238
- Look at that.

00:04:04.238 --> 00:04:06.063
I was in Chicago for a
like a week and a half.

00:04:06.063 --> 00:04:07.157
And it was freezing.

00:04:07.157 --> 00:04:08.850
And that entire week is just a wash.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.374
I owe $47.

00:04:10.374 --> 00:04:11.909
I think I'll give it to Saint Jude,

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:13.452
the children's hospital.

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:14.110
- That's a safe bet.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:15.580
- [Voiceover] You owe a dollar.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.376
- That was so close.

00:04:16.376 --> 00:04:18.082
- You must have done 10,000

00:04:18.082 --> 00:04:19.383
almost every day.

00:04:19.383 --> 00:04:20.317
- I tried.

00:04:20.317 --> 00:04:21.045
- That's amazing.

00:04:21.045 --> 00:04:21.784
- That's the difference.

00:04:21.784 --> 00:04:23.047
If you try,
- (laughing)

00:04:23.047 --> 00:04:24.356
you'll almost make it.

00:04:24.356 --> 00:04:26.197
- So who you're giving nine bucks to?

00:04:26.197 --> 00:04:28.313
- I feel like giving them $9 is a joke.

00:04:28.313 --> 00:04:30.537
- Maybe you just throw $9

00:04:30.537 --> 00:04:31.934
on one of our charities.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.033
- I think I'm gonna go
with sick little kids.

00:04:33.469 --> 00:04:34.281
- Again,

00:04:34.281 --> 00:04:35.106
that's the safe bet.

00:04:35.106 --> 00:04:36.816
(all laughing)

00:04:39.526 --> 00:04:41.441
- I like feel like I probably will.

00:04:41.441 --> 00:04:42.861
It's slightly obsessive to

00:04:42.861 --> 00:04:43.833
like constantly
- Yes.

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:45.084
- know what number it is.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.871
Like a little game
you're playing every day.

00:04:46.871 --> 00:04:48.940
- I think the only thing
that I did slightly more

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.681
with this is like always take the stairs

00:04:50.681 --> 00:04:51.655
when I was at work.

00:04:51.655 --> 00:04:53.170
Doing a little bit of extra effort.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.158
You know, the bare minimum extra.

00:04:55.158 --> 00:04:56.436
- (laughing)
- I'm doing that.

00:04:56.436 --> 00:04:57.433
- I'm definitely not gonna feel bad

00:04:57.433 --> 00:04:58.974
if I don't hit 10,000 any more.

00:04:58.974 --> 00:05:00.151
I'm not gonna stress about it.

00:05:00.151 --> 00:05:01.248
But I'll at least try.

00:05:01.248 --> 00:05:02.411
- Alright, we did it!

00:05:02.411 --> 00:05:04.210
- [Voiceover] Whoo, whoo!

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:05.561
(hands clapping)

00:05:05.561 --> 00:05:07.227
- [Voiceover] My life has changed.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:08.793
(squeaking sign)

